<% content_for :title, "Demos · yrby" %>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
  <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-zinc-100 sm:text-5xl">Demos</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-zinc-400">
    Each demo syncs a different kind of Yjs document through the same Rails
    app. Each room is one record with a document per demo, declared with
    <code>has_collaborative_document</code>. The shape demos use
    <code>RoomChannel</code>, yrby-rails' own document channel, which saves
    every update, sends it to everyone in the room, and has no code for any
    particular demo. The Lexxy demo uses <code>LexxyChannel</code>,
    lexxy-realtime's channel, which also renders the room's body to HTML after
    each change. Every demo page has a panel that shows what Ruby reads from
    the saved state.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-zinc-400">
    New to yrby? Start with the <a class="text-accent underline" href="/examples/document">record-backed editor</a>.
    It runs the quickstart code on a single record, with
    <code>collaborative_document_tag</code> and a CodeMirror editor.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-amber-500/25 bg-amber-500/8 px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-amber-200/90">
    Each demo opens in a new room with its own URL. Share the URL to edit
    together. Anyone with the link can edit the room. A room is deleted after
    <%= Limits::ROOM_IDLE_TTL / 3600 %> hours with no edits and nobody
    connected, so please don't paste anything private.
  </p>

  <ul class="demo-list">
    <% @demos.each do |demo| %>
      <li>
        <%# A POST, because each click creates a new room for that visitor. %>
        <%= button_to demo.title, demo_open_path(demo.slug), authenticity_token: false %>
        <code><%= demo.shape %></code>
        <span><%= demo.blurb %></span>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>
